item~ function src/phext.rs :: get_subspace_coordinates :: pub fn get_subspace_coordinates(subspace: &[u8], target: Coordinate) -> (usize, usize, Coordinate) { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn get_subspace_coordinates  finds the start and end offsets for the given coordinate  The walker only moves on a dimension break, so its comparisons with `target` are redone only at the start and right after a break, and the scan stops once the end is known (stage 2): nothing after that point can change the result. Earlier versions compared full coordinates on every byte and always scanned to the end of the document. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment
