item~ function src/phext.rs :: append :: pub fn append(input: String, location: Coordinate, scroll: &str) -> Option<String> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn append  Appends `scroll` at `location`, which must sort strictly after the document's last non-empty scroll. The result is the input with only a delimiter run and the new content added at its end — a host can write just that suffix to a file opened in append mode and sync once.  Returns None when the scroll is empty (empty scrolls do not exist) or `location` does not sort after the document's end. Trailing delimiter bytes in the input encode only empty scrolls, so they are dropped first and never shift the appended scroll's address.  On None the append was rejected; the input String was consumed, so pass a clone if the caller needs it after a rejected append.  The document's end is located with `last_scroll_coordinate`, a backward delimiter scan over the bytes — existing text is never re-tokenized, so a call's cost tracks the delimiter run at the end of the document, not the size of the document. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment
